<h2>quickest start</h2>
<ol>
<li>check to see if python is already installed.<ul>
<li>in the terminal, the python interpreter is accessed with the command <code>python</code>. You can exit the interpreter with Ctrl-D.</li>
<li>If not available, install through your system package manager or by <a href="https://www.python.org/downloads/">downloading</a></li>
<li>The package is probably called <code>python</code></li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>create a file <code>hello.py</code> which contains the line <code>print(&quot;Hello World!&quot;)</code></li>
<li>run the command <code>python hello.py</code><ul>
<li>should see output <code>Hello World!</code></li>
</ul>
</li>
</ol>

